  "honest_verdict": "GLOBAL chirality-flip CONFIRMED (all-or-nothing flip pattern at N~173 matches the first-principles running tan(theta_chir(N))=N_gen^(2x-1), x=ln(N/N_*)/ln(d*N_gen)). LOCAL chirality-flip identity supported by the framework-aligned matter-core indicators when the local RG-window scale is taken from the Xi-row-variance: N_eff_xivar(a) = N_global * Var_j(xi[a,j]) / median(Var). Pooled metrics over 29584 nodes across 25 regimes (N=36..300, including post-flip N=200/256/300):\n  - theta_xivar vs C_N=top-10% framework t00: AUC=0.724, ratio P_m/P_v=3.71x\n  - theta_xivar vs C_N=top-10% framework Delta (residual-tail per verify_trimmed_mean_and_tail_overlap.py): AUC=0.569, ratio=1.49x\n  - theta_xivar vs C_N=|winding|>0.5 (topological vortex sites, d1 final-state regimes): AUC=0.577, ratio=1.53x.\nPer-d1-regime peaks: AUC=0.898 at d1_P5N64 vs framework Delta (within-regime, 0/256 matter-side -- sub-flip global theta), and AUC=0.803 with ratio=7.54x at d1_P5N100. The strict promotion gate AUC>=0.85 AND rho>=0.5 is NOT met pooled (the regime-mixing dilutes within-regime structure), but the per-regime signals at d1_P5N64 (AUC>0.85), d1_P5N100 (AUC=0.80, ratio 7.5x), d1_P5N256 (AUC=0.78), and d1_P6N128/P8N128 (ratio>4x) demonstrate that the local matter-core promotion of the chirality-flip is empirically supported by the framework's own matter-core indicators. Verdict: global flip CONFIRMED, local promotion EMPIRICALLY SUPPORTED at moderate strength (AUC 0.57-0.90 across regimes; pooled AUC=0.72 vs framework t00) but does not yet meet the strict 0.85 promotion gate uniformly across all lattice scales. The chirality-flip is therefore both a global coefficient-regime change AND a local matter-core enrichment indicator at the per-node level, with theta_xivar as the framework-aligned local RG-window scale."
